course: dictionary
lesson: 12922
title: Where words come from
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words look strange because their spelling is older than the way we say them now. Etymological means to do with etymology, the history of where a word comes from and how its meaning and spelling have changed. «The b in doubt is silent, but it was added to match the Latin word dubitare.» That story is an etymological explanation.
explain: Etymology is the study of word histories. When you look up a word, the entry may have an etymological note at the end. It tells you the word's roots, the older words it came from. Phrases like «etymological roots» and «etymological note» all point to this same kind of history.
explain: Knowing a word's history can help you remember its spelling. If you learn that doubt comes from dubitare, the silent b makes more sense. You do not have to remember it as a random rule. Ask yourself: where did this word start, and what did it look like long ago?
fact: Etymological means to do with the history of where words come from.
fact: Etymology is the study of how words began and how their meanings and forms have changed.
fact: «Doubt» has a silent b because it was added to match the Latin word dubitare.
fact: An etymological note at the end of a dictionary entry explains a word's history.
fact: An etymological explanation tells you why a word is spelled the way it is.
exercise: «The etymological note at the end of the entry told Mia why the word has a silent b.» What does etymological mean here? | To do with counting letters | *To do with the history of where a word comes from | To do with the colour of a page | To do with reading aloud
exercise: Which word would you look up in an etymological dictionary to learn why it has a silent b? | garden | jump | *doubt | happy
exercise: Ravi asks, «Why is there a b in doubt if we don't say it?» Which kind of explanation answers him best? | *An etymological explanation, which tells the word's history | A list of opposite words | A picture of a worried face | A rhyme that sounds the same
test: «The teacher said the spelling came from Latin, so she gave an etymological explanation.» What is an etymological explanation? | *A story about where a word came from and how it changed | A game with rhyming words | A short poem about spelling | A rule for adding -ing
test: Which phrase names a dictionary that shows the history of words? | word search book | rhyming dictionary | *etymological dictionary | picture dictionary
exam: «The silent b in doubt was added because of the Latin word dubitare.» This is an example of which kind of explanation? | A synonym for a harder word | A list of rhyming words | A phonics clue about sounds | *An etymological explanation
